{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428798-the-starlight-bridge-a-shipyard-of-dreams","id":1428798,"title":"The Starlight Bridge, a Shipyard of Dreams","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-17T13:41:59-08:00","id":1428798,"title":"The Starlight Bridge, a Shipyard of Dreams","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spun out of crystal and dreams and hopes, the Starlight bridge is a fragile seeming structure composed out of translucent, shifting and ebbing material that seemed to change shape before your very perceptions. Situated right at the hyperspace lane of Marjani, the Starlight bridge is a port and shipyard without peer for the local light years. Capable of cranking out ships from the ether-nebulae around it, the Bridge serves as the last port of call before explorers enter the great unknown, or as the staging ground for the construction of entirely new ships. The ever-shifting material flexes and transforms, allowing the Bridge to service the smallest Dagger-craft to the largest Titan-crawler. Manse functions enable it to create ships an order of magnitude faster than any mundane port. Filled to the brim with food, supplies, and a large populace, it is a popular rest stop.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Of course, with so much money, cargo, trade, and opportunities to be had, the entire station is a hotbed of intrigue. The heartstone bearer rarely appears in public without his dragonblooded body guards. The manse's slaved defenses are ready to take down or eject any interloper who falls out of favor. All things are traded within, from drugs, to contraband, to rare animals, to human souls. Demons, gods, Exalted, the odd Primordial race, are allowed onto the station, save for those who are hopelessly hostile or belligerent. The station itself though as tough as anything else, is still built out of spun glass. Damaging the manse in any significant way is grounds for immediate ejection by all factions. Scratching the surface is allowed, but damaging one of the superstructures is *not* allowed. Thus, high powered weapons are not in use by the inhabitants. Instead, there is a focus on close hand to hand combat, precision sniper fire, nasty poison, grapples and nets, and the odd assasination. Think less 'explosive Dawn' and more 'Sneaky Night'.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Manse traits:</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Palace Sized</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Fragile</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Reduced Hearthstone</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Number of facilities: 9</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Facilities:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Docks:</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The shining docks of the Starlight Bridge contain many wondrous tools of gleaming crystal and solid light. Holograms appear on the ship, only to suddenly coalesce from raw essence into solid matter. Crystalline tools turn the work of hours into mere minutes. All attempts to repair or construct ships and other vessels will be reduced in time. Ships with repairs that would require a refit of months can be repaired in mere weeks or even days. Ships that would require years to build can be made in a Season. This is one of the most prized assets of the Starlight Bridge, and is a prize for anybody who wishes to save their precious time.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Bound Servants</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Glowing automatons that resemble masses of crystalline rock. These automatons clean, patrol the facility, repair any damage, and also assist in any shipboard duties from repairing ships to helping to unload cargo. When the station itself suffers great damage, they will turn on the interloper in great numbers, swarming him with a battlegroup of Might 1 and Elite Drill that cannot be routed, and constantly regenerates itself from the walls.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Storage (Haze of Maze):</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Bridge produces it's own goods, and sometimes production overshoots consumption. The excess gets stored in the storage area, a maze of ever-shifting tunnels burrowed into Elsewhere where you only need to turn a corner to get any section. The Storage area stores foodstuffs, spare parts, machines... and collateral. Some ships are valuable and shipowners don't have enough liquid cash. Sometimes a privateer doesn't have enough money and has to pawn some of his artifacts to restore his ship from a cored out hulk. Either way these need to be kept. To get the normal supplies is easy. To get the collateral is something else. Either get the manse bearer (and beat his DB bodyguards) and use the hearthstone to command the maze to spit out its secrets, or navigate the maze (which is requires 15 successes on a difficulty 5 + hearthstone bearer's essence roll), avoiding the traps and the patrolling ground in the first place. This is something that requires not only good stealth (there is zero cover and the bright lights give a +3 awareness bonus) but the ability to even navigate the maze at all and avoid the traps.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Observation Area (Inner-eye workings)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Under the command of a the hearthstone bearer and a rudimentary intelligence, the Inner-eye stretches across the entirety of the Starlight Bridge's inner surface, checking for hostility, fae, the dead, or any other scum. It is able to remotely observe any area not blocked by something like Private Plaza of Downcast Eyes, and reflexively has a read intentions on 'hostile intent towards the station', with 10 dice with autosuccesses equal to the hearthstone bearer's essence. It can record and play any event that it observes, letting it be the final word in the impromptu courts of the Starlight Bridge on whether or not to throw out someone into space.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Artillery (Prismatic Beams)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Deadly beams of force that can project from any section of the Starlight Bridge. The area is remote, and not too far from the Fae-holdings, which means raids. A fleet of ships patrols the area, but sometimes they are overwhelmed or the foe strikes by surprise. When this occurs, the ships retreat into the covering fire of the Starlight, deadly beams of force erupting from space itself to pummel its attackers. This has only enraged the fae and they dearly seek to destroy it for it is a gateway to other more vulnerable worlds behind in the hyperspace lanes, if not for pride itself. Perhaps they are willing to send in internal saboteurs, or even hire a group of Exalted to help condemn a space station and the hundreds of thousands within to a gruesome death by soul-sucking...</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Multiplicity Factory (Workshop)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A workshop that has traded in its ability to produce artifacts, for extensive flexibility. The multiplicity factory focuses on good, low maintenance, and workhorse technology that ships plunging into the oceans of madness would need. It cannot produce artifacts, only alchemical products at best. Capable of making food rations, paint, combat drugs, blasters, plasma cannons, first aid kits, lights, and wooden chairs, the Multiplicity factory produces products that are sold in the marketplace. Prices jump and drop depending on the people entering and exiting, and their destinations. A ship travelling to the Umbral worlds would make the price of lanterns skyrocket, while someone about to explore the venom tainted worlds of the Hadex Crossing would cause the price of anti-venom to jump. Of course, this serves as an excellent way to gain a lot of money, or an enterprising bureaucrat to leverage his way into favors, political deals, and maybe even destroy the competition. Supplies are a serious business. It also cannot produce everything at once, and it's production cycles are a sought after commodity. Someone with intelligence and quick wit can easily make up for the gap in the supply with his own skills.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Etheric Tap (Farm)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A tap capable of transmuting raw potential into solidified matter. This serves as raw material for the multiplicity factory, letting it produce something from effectively nothing. It produces unfinished goods, ranging from raw meat and grain, to crude metals, to feedstock for chemical industries. An entire community has arisen from making up the shortfalls in the multiplicity factory's production by making the goods themselves, eking out a living making obscure or extremely specific supplies. Which of course can serve as a place to buy black market contraband or things even the station's master finds detestable.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Entertainment</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Life aboard the station is precarious. Money changing hands bring murder and death like no other. The fragility of the station means that you can hear the superstrcuture creak, knowing that a single bad blow can leave you exposed to the vacuum of space. There actually <i>isn't</i> much to do. Constant movement of ships in and out means that sometimes, hearts yearn for those who are not there. The general lack of security leads to malaise. Thus, anything that will distract them is welcome. People play poker, strip poker, games of all kind, from kicking a ball to paintball guns. The current entertainment is for storytelling. They love a good storyteller. Especially one that has romance. A particularly skilled one might find himself the darling of the hour, with welcomes and free drinks everywhere, and of course, be in favor of the court and receive special privileges, ranging from having their ships having priority in repairs to having control of the production cycles, to even access to its secret archives to show who entered, who went on which ship, and which ship went to where...</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T15:44:09-08:00","id":1428810,"title":"","content":"Always nice to see more Sci-fi Exalted.<br /> <br /> This an original setting you making?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T15:58:08-08:00","id":1428813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428798-the-starlight-bridge-a-shipyard-of-dreams?p=1428810#post1428810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Always nice to see more Sci-fi Exalted.<br /> <br /> This an original setting you making?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. More 'science fantasy' than your own 'sci-fi'. The Exalted are still irreplaceable, unmatchable miracles.<br /> <br /> It's just that after a few crazy-ass sorcerous workings and universal reboots, the multiverse got a hell of a lot more magical. Several thousand alchemicals, and a million dragonblooded. And a shitload more sorcerers. And the primordial races came back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}